      "fact": "As of August 2018, there were no credible media reports indicating that Donald Trump Jr. had been formally charged with a crime.",
      "source_date": "2018-08-01"
    }
  ],
  "reasoning": "Based on the status of the investigation as of August 2018, Donald Trump Jr. had not been questioned by Special Counsel Robert Mueller [1] and no charges had been filed against him [2]. While he had testified to congressional committees regarding the Trump Tower meeting [3], his legal team expressed confidence in the information provided [4], and there were no reports of formal charges at that time [5]. Given that the investigation was ongoing but had not yet resulted in charges against him by August, and considering the pattern of charges being filed against associates like Manafort and Flynn, there was no public evidence at the time to suggest a charge would be imminent before Christmas 2018. The absence of any indictment or formal charge by August 2018, combined with the lack of new evidence presented to the public suggesting an imminent indictment, supports the prediction that he would not be charged by the end of the year.",
